From 5007888da4b4e0f08bb3c124e8a10a99a9c903fc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lynxifyy <297587416+Lynxifyy@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 18:16:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add a C ABI for the replay service

ReplayService was C++ only, so a host that dlopen's libBerryAPI.so - a launcher's
native preloader - could not load a replay or drive playback without linking the whole
C++ surface. berry/replay_c.h closes that gap the same way berry/seam.h closed it for
the world seam: a plain C struct of function pointers obtained from
BERRY_GetReplayApi().

Fail-closed, matching the seam's contract:
  * BERRY_GetReplayApi returns null before attach, so a host cannot drive a replay on
    an engine that is not running.
  * The struct carries size and abi_version; the host checks both against
    BERRY_ReplayStructSize()/BERRY_ReplayAbiVersion() before calling a pointer, so a
    layout drift is caught by a number.
  * Every call that can fail returns a named status and writes nothing on failure.

The surface covers load/save/unload, the replay summary (ticks, sections, records,
payload bytes, fingerprint), play/pause/stop/seek/set_speed/playback, the local player
id and a status line. test_replay_c pins the whole contract on the host: the version
and size agree, the surface is refused before attach, every call fails closed with a
named status, a malformed replay is refused, and save refuses with nothing loaded.
Verified exported in the shared library (nm -D) and the dlopen smoke test still passes.
